**What the draft argues.** It opens with Pratt's 2015 GQ line about his heavy, fun Andy Dwyer years: "That image that I was casting, to convince people that I was okay... Now I have less fun. I focus more." The thread from there is something he learned at 19, selling coupons door to door: "what you're selling is yourself and you're selling your attitude." The draft types him as a 3, medium confidence. The key test against 7 is which one he protects when fun and looking successful pull apart, and his record keeps choosing the look:
- He hid the failed sales job from his hometown.
- He chose the fat-guy persona because it was "paying better," then dropped it once it cost him a role.
- James Gunn said he "always has to juggle to entertain everybody."

